  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788548",
      "title": "We Need More Flexible Components!",
      "lectureOrder": 30,
      "videoOrder": 26,
      "sourceHash": "385a4fab821f869d89a0f7cb2af6dd369701df8ddd5dc4080acf210d2094b2e1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.1,
          "en": "At this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "we covered a lot of crucial Angular concepts already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 9.427,
          "en": "But of course, the demo application we are working on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.427,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "didn't make too much progress.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "But it is of course super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 16.77,
          "en": "to have this solid foundation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.77,
          "end": 18.885,
          "en": "and to know about all these core concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.885,
          "end": 21.933,
          "en": "I did explain over the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "That being said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "I now wanna continue working on this UI though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 30.93,
          "en": "And for example, the idea with this user here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.93,
          "end": 33.404,
          "en": "is not to have a single user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.404,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "that changes whenever we click on them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "but instead to have a list of users here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "where we have multiple user items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.85,
          "end": 44.835,
          "en": "which when we click on them, load their tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.835,
          "end": 47.343,
          "en": "which should then show up on the right here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "And therefore as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "I wanna work on that list of users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "And therefore, I first wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "that this user component can be used multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "so that we can use one and the same user component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "multiple times but with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "Because that's another big advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "of this Components approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 76.119,
          "en": "You don't just split your user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.119,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "into those building blocks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "hence simplifying those individual building blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "But you also have reusable building blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "And of course, not every component needs to be reused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "The HeaderComponent, for example, is only used once here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 100.76599999999999,
          "en": "but some components are reused like this UserComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.76599999999999,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "which is meant to be output multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 105.453,
          "en": "with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 109.38,
          "en": "Now of course, we can go to the AppComponent here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.38,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "and simply copy and paste this list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "with the UserComponent multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 117.363,
          "en": "to output multiple users like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 121.995,
          "en": "But if we do that, it's always the same user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.995,
          "end": 125.22,
          "en": "at least initially until we change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.22,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "And it's always the same user initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 129.66,
          "en": "because in the UserComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.66,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "we initially calculate this random index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 137.13,
          "en": "and this is done only once when this file is first parsed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.13,
          "end": 139.71,
          "en": "And then, we use this random index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 144.71,
          "en": "to select one random user, which we use as a starting value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.32999999999998,
          "en": "And that's of course not the idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.32999999999998,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "Instead, I actually don't wanna pick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "any random index or random user at all here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 157.65,
          "en": "And I also don't wanna change the selected user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.65,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "when we click on them so we can get rid of this code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 165.48,
          "en": "I also don't need a selected user here at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.48,
          "end": 168.87,
          "en": "because the idea is not to show different users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 171.39600000000002,
          "en": "inside of the UserComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.39600000000002,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "So we can get rid of all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 175.953,
          "en": "and clean up this UserComponent class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 180.37,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, also get rid of this import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "and get rid of the compute and signal functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 185.823,
          "en": "that are being imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 189.717,
          "en": "Because instead, I want to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.717,
          "end": 193.221,
          "en": "my app UserComponent configurable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.221,
          "end": 198.221,
          "en": "so that we can set attributes, properties to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 201.99,
          "en": "on that component here, on that element tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.99,
          "end": 205.29,
          "en": "just as we can do it on built-in elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.29,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "That would be a nice feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 210.57,
          "en": "because that would then allow us to really reuse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.57,
          "end": 214.98,
          "en": "one and the same component, but with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.98,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "And that is of course, a crucial feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 219.963,
          "en": "that is supported by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
